{{Quote|What you are proposing could be construed as treason.|translated=1|Shu Mai, to Dooku|<ref name="Attack of the Clones" />}}
'''Shu Mai''' was a [[Gender|female]] [[Gossam]] who served as [[Presidente]] of the [[Commerce Guild]] during the [[Republic Era|final]] [[Standard year|years]] of the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> During the [[Separatist Crisis]], she attended a meeting with [[Count]] [[Dooku]] and the heads of other noted corporate holdings on [[Geonosis]] to discuss joining the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="Attack of the Clones" /> Though Mai showed misgivings about the situation, stating that the proposal could be viewed as [[treason]], she was the only one to do so and ultimately [[Geonosian accord|pledged]] the forces of the Commerce Guild to the Separatist cause and gained a seat on the [[Executive Separatist Council|Separatist Council]] as a result.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> Despite the Commerce Guild not openly backing the Separatists, Shu Mai's provided [[DSD1 dwarf spider droid|DSD1 dwarf]] and [[OG-9 homing spider droid]]s to fight for their cause during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Updated and Expanded">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref>

Towards the end of the war during the [[Outer Rim Sieges]], Shu Mai led the occupation of [[Felucia]], and while there attempted to persuade the local [[Felucian]]s to align with the Separatists Shu kidnapped [[Ormo Hyn]], a relative of a pro-Republic Felucian leader. [[Jedi Master]] [[Aayla Secura]] and the [[327th Star Corps]] were dispatched to the planet with the objective of capturing Shu Mai and freeing her hostage. Before the Republic forces were able to engage her droid army, Shu had already been evacuated to [[Utapau]] alongside the rest of the Executive Council.<ref name="Battles">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]''</ref>

Shu was present when General [[Grievous]] arrived following his defeat at the [[Battle of Coruscant]]. Under the instructions of [[Sith Lord|Lord]] [[Darth Sidious|Sidious]], Grevious sent the entire Council to the planet [[Mustafar]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]] under the pretext of their own protection from the advancing Republic forces. There they remained sequestered until the promised arrival of Sidious's new apprentice: [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], who was to take care of them. When Lord Vader [[Mission to Mustafar|arrived]] he promptly [[Death|slaughtered]] Shu Mai alongside the rest of the council before transmitting shut down command to all Separatist droid forces, effectively ending the Clone Wars.<ref name="Revenge of the Sith" />

==Personality and traits==
Concerned only with wealth, status, and power, Mai worked her way up the Commerce Guild using aggressive and unscrupulous tactics until no rivals stood in her way of becoming President.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> Her obsessions remained when she became a member of the Separatist Council.<ref name="Force Collection">{{ForceCollection|Shu Mai|star=2}}</ref> She opted to join the Confederacy after being convinced by Dooku on Geonosis, despite her initial doubts.<ref name="Attack of the Clones" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Shu Mai first appeared in ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the [[2002]] film [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']].<ref name="Attack of the Clones" /> Before that, Mai appeared in the 2002 [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] novel ''[[The Approaching Storm]]'' written by [[Alan Dean Foster]].<ref name="Approaching Storm">''[[The Approaching Storm]]''</ref> Concept art of the final design of the character was done by [[Dermot Power]], while other artwork was also done by [[Iain McCaig]].<ref name="ArtofII">''[[The Art of Star Wars Episode II: Attack of the Clones]]''</ref> She was realized as a computer generated character and a maquette was created of her.<ref name="DB old">{{DB|character|shumai|Mai, Shu}}</ref> [[Wikipedia:Shumai|Shu mai]] (燒賣) is also the name of a popular type of [[Wikipedia:Dim sum|Chinese dumpling]].<ref name="Separatists at Birth">{{InsiderCite|69|Behind the Magic}}</ref>

In the [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith Illustrated Screenplay|illustrated screenplay]] of ''Revenge of the Sith'', Mai lasts longer than in the final cut. Rather than getting killed almost immediately, she runs to the conference room along with [[Wat Tambor]] only to be cut down by Vader after Tambor's death.<ref name="Ep. III Illustrated Screenplay">[[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith Illustrated Screenplay|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith Illustrated Screenplay'']]</ref>

